{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Input Density.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Input Density.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"input density input density","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Input Density.md","fileName":"Input Density.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Input Density","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 15:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Mechanics and Rules]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Mechanics and Rules","Physical Input Layer","Game Verb","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Input Density.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Input Density.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"input density input density","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Input Density.md","fileName":"Input Density.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Input Density","heading":"Input Density","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Input density is the amount of meaningful interaction expressed through a compact [[Physical Input Layer]]. A single button can represent several related phases when pressing, holding, and releasing it each have a clear role.\n\nDense input can reduce hand movement, mispresses, and memorization while keeping important [[Game Verb|verbs]] prominent. Density is useful when the mappings remain coherent; compressing unrelated actions onto one control can instead make the system harder to predict.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Mechanics and Rules","Physical Input Layer","Game Verb","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Input Density.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Input Density.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"input density input density","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Input Density.md","fileName"